mill

# .mill/ is agent runtime state and is not tracked — with two exceptions.
# Role definitions and the phase gates are source, not state: a delegated
# worktree is created with `git worktree add`, which only materialises
# tracked files, so anything an agent needs to read must be versioned.
# Note the trailing /*: git cannot re-include anything inside a directory
# that is itself excluded, so the contents are excluded and two subtrees
# are added back.
# .mill/ holds both source and runtime state. Since the Go CLI was retired
# (ADR 0006) the source half is most of it: roles, checks, skills and docs are
# the product. Exclude the runtime directories explicitly and track the rest,
# so that forgetting produces a tracked file that should not be — which is
# visible — rather than a missing one, which is not. The previous allowlist
# silently dropped .mill/skills/using-mill.md, the skill this project now is.
/.mill/ledger/
/.mill/worktrees/
/.mill/logs/
/.mill/state/
/.mill/artifacts/
# Note: .mill/phases/ is NOT excluded. FRDs, specs and tasks are source — a
# delegated worktree materialises only tracked files, so an untracked frd.md
# never reaches the role that needs it (#128).
/.mill/memory/
/.mill/role
/.mill/map.json
/.mill/session.md
/.mill/placeholder

# Session exports from the agent harness (multi-MB HTML transcripts)
omp-session-*.html

# Scratch specs and working notes, not part of the tracked history
/local/
.commandcode/
